* r1_isense -- low-side shunt sense amplifier, one channel (r1_isense_ch) and the two-channel top (r1_isense)
* IHP SG13G2, schematic-level SPICE source (hand-written; no xschem view in this step).
*
* Transfer (ideal network):  OUTP - OUTN = G * ((ISP - ISN) - VPED)
*   G    = RF/RIN = 14 (14 RIN units in each feedback arm)
*   VPED = VREF * RIN/RP = 1.05 V / 26 = 40.38 mV (input-referred pedestal)
*   -20 mV .. +100 mV  ->  -0.85 V .. +0.83 V differential; output common mode = VCM (0.6 V)
*
* Amplifier: fully differential two-stage Miller OTA.
*   Stage 1 on VDDA (3.3 V): thick-oxide PMOS input pair (input common mode near 0 V), folded cascode,
*            CMFB on part of the folding sinks.
*   Stage 2 on VDD (1.2 V core): thick-oxide NMOS common source (its gate may see up to 3.3 V),
*            thin-oxide PMOS current-source load. OUTP/OUTN can therefore never exceed VDD (<= 1.32 V):
*            the outputs are safe for the thin-oxide ADC multiplexer and comparator inputs.
* Offset cancellation: auto-zero of the whole channel with offset storage on an auxiliary input pair (AZ servo).
*   AZ is run only while the shunt carries no current (low-side FET off, outside the dead time; r1_gate knows
*   the phase), so ISP - ISN = 0 without any switch in the signal path.
*   AZ (az high, 3.3 V level after the level shifter):
*     - the output ends of both RF arms are moved from OUTN/OUTP to VCM (series thick-NMOS switches, 40 um,
*       about 25 Ohm in normal mode against 56 kOhm), so the network sees exactly Vod = 0 at 0.6 V;
*       the amplifier outputs are free during AZ;
*     - both pedestal arms are opened at the summing nodes (pedestal off, network symmetric);
*   AZH (azh high, inside AZ): hold caps CH1/CH2 connect to the stage-1 outputs x1a/x1b; the auxiliary
*     pair (gm_aux ~ gm1/12) closes a unity servo that nulls the stage-1 output. The stored correction cancels
*     the OTA offset AND the resistor-network error at Vod = 0 (output common mode 0.6 V through mismatched
*     RF/RIN ratios), so the output at zero shunt current is -G * VPED after AZ.
*   Sequence (set by r1_ctrl, at least one 33 ns clock cycle apart): azh falls first, then az falls.
*   The output is not valid during AZ and for the recovery time after it; r1_safe blanks over that window.
* Device conventions: PMOS bulks to their supply (input, aux and CMFB pairs: bulk = own tail, separate n-wells), NMOS bulks to vss, rppd/rhigh body to vss, mm_ok=1 everywhere.

.subckt r1_ls in vdd vdda vss out outb
* 1.2 V -> 3.3 V level shifter (thin-oxide inverter for the complement, thick-oxide cross-coupled stage)
XMIP inb in vdd vdd sg13_lv_pmos w=1u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XMIN inb in vss vss sg13_lv_nmos w=0.5u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XMN1 a in vss vss sg13_hv_nmos w=4u l=0.45u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XMN2 b inb vss vss sg13_hv_nmos w=4u l=0.45u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XMP1 a b vdda vdda sg13_hv_pmos w=0.6u l=0.5u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XMP2 b a vdda vdda sg13_hv_pmos w=0.6u l=0.5u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
* b is high when in is high
XMB1P outb b vdda vdda sg13_hv_pmos w=2u l=0.5u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XMB1N outb b vss vss sg13_hv_nmos w=1u l=0.45u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XMB2P out outb vdda vdda sg13_hv_pmos w=2u l=0.5u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XMB2N out outb vss vss sg13_hv_nmos w=1u l=0.45u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
.ends r1_ls

